Date: Thu, 25 Jun 2026 13:34:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03994/11362] [outer-loop] Measure L2 fix stack on lp85: does
 NOT bank L2; wall is upstream (L2 reinduction reliability), not goal quality

Focused reproduction-gated lp85 probe (single game/arm, budget 400) with default-ON truncation +
goal-repair active. Result: max_depth=1, l2_reproduced=False. But the failure mode REFUTES the
"loose goal won't reproduce" prediction: the L2 level-up reinduction proposer_FAILED (no valid code
after 3 retries on the REAL lp85 L2 prompt), so the goal-repair never engaged (it is downstream of
induction success). The agent DOES pass the exemplar and _call_induce routes through the code-only
induce (no wiring gap); the online induction succeeded (wrote a real "no cell==3" predicate); and
the code-only path is 3/3 reliable on the SYNTHETIC prompt -- but the real lp85 L2 reinduction prompt
fails code-gen. Bisected wall, in order: (1) real-L2-prompt code-gen reliability [immediate];
(2) goal quality / structural-alignment goal [downstream]. n=1 caveat: next step is to capture the
real L2 prompt + raw output and measure valid-rate to separate prompt-specific failure from variance.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
